CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* size: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* no element destroyed yet: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* element value: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] .* destroyed with the variable: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Fixed: the backing array (initializer_list_backing_array, cpp_typecheck_
conversions.cpp) is a static-lifetime symbol whose elements are constructed
in place where the list is evaluated; goto conversion now destroys them
when the initializer_list object it initializes goes out of scope.
g++ 13 (-fsanitize=address,undefined) and clang++ 18 accept this program,
and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
